---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const page = {
  "title": "Privacy policy — Ey-aye",
  "description": "How Ey-aye (Loftsoft) collects, uses and protects personal data, and your rights under UK GDPR.",
  "path": "/privacy"
};
---
<Base {...page}>
<section class="wrap legal">
<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
<p class="updated">Last updated 6 November 2026</p>
<p>Ey-aye is a trading name of Loftsoft, run by Paul Lofthouse ("we", "us"), 7 Oakridge View, Harrogate, HG3 2WH. We are the data controller for the personal data described here. Questions go to <a href="mailto:paul@ey-aye.co.uk">paul@ey-aye.co.uk</a>.</p>
<h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Enquiries.</strong> When you use the contact form or email us, we collect your name, business name, email address and whatever you tell us. We use it to reply to you and, if you become a client, to do the work. Lawful basis: our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries, then the contract with you.</li>
<li><strong>Bookings.</strong> If you book a look-round through our booking tool, the tool's provider collects the details needed to make the appointment and shares them with us. Their privacy policy applies to their processing.</li>
<li><strong>Client work.</strong> If we build or configure something for your business, we may process personal data held in your systems (customers, bookings, invoices) on your behalf and under your instructions. For that data you are the controller and we are a processor, and our written agreement with you covers it.</li>
<li><strong>Website use.</strong> Our hosting provider (Cloudflare) keeps standard server logs, including IP addresses, for security and to keep the site running. When you arrive from a tagged link (for example one we posted on social media, or an ad), we count which link it was, the page you landed on and your country. We don't record your IP address, set cookies or store anything in your browser to do it. We do not run advertising trackers on this site.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Who we share it with</h2>
<p>Only the suppliers we need to run the business, each under their own data protection terms: our hosting provider (Cloudflare), our booking tool, our email provider, and our accountant for invoicing. We do not sell personal data and we do not use it to train AI models.</p>
<h2>AI tools</h2>
<p>We use AI services in our work. Where we do, we use business accounts whose terms exclude training on the data, and we do not put client or customer data into consumer AI tools. The same rule applies to anything we build for you.</p>
<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>Enquiries for up to two years from the last contact. Client records for six years after the work ends, because tax law requires it. Server logs for a short rolling period set by the hosting provider.</p>
<h2>Where it's stored</h2>
<p>In the UK or EU where we can. Some suppliers process data in the United States under the UK's international data transfer rules.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You can ask to see the personal data we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, object to or restrict how we use it, and ask for a copy in a portable format. Email <a href="mailto:paul@ey-aye.co.uk">paul@ey-aye.co.uk</a> and we'll reply within a month. If you're not happy with how we've handled something, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.</p>
</section>
</Base>
